---
title: BLT Salad
description: A hearty shredded kale salad with crispy bacon and juicy cherry tomatoes, tossed in a creamy homemade Greek yogurt ranch dressing.
course: Salad
cuisine: American
servings: 4
prep time: 15 minutes
cook time: 10 minutes
source: https://www.howsweeteats.com/2017/03/blt-shredded-kale-salad-greek-yogurt-ranch/
image: https://www.howsweeteats.com/wp-content/uploads/2017/03/kale-BLT-salad-I-howsweeteats.com-8.jpg
tags: [salad, kale, bacon, healthy]
---

Place @kale{1%large head}(stems removed and shredded) in a #large bowl{}, drizzle with @olive oil{1%tbsp}, and add @salt{1/4%tsp} and @pepper{1/4%tsp}. Massage the oil in by hand for a few minutes, then set aside.

Heat a #skillet{} over medium-low, add the @thick-cut bacon{4%slices}(chopped), and cook until totally crispy, stirring occasionally and the fat is rendered, about ~{10%minutes}.

To make the dressing, blend @greek yogurt{1/3%cup}, @mayonnaise{2%tbsp}, @parsley{1%tsp}(freshly chopped), @dill{1%tsp}(freshly chopped), @garlic{1%clove}(minced), @worcestershire sauce{1/2%tsp}, @white vinegar{1/4%tsp}, @smoked paprika{1/4%tsp}, @onion powder{1/8%tsp}, @salt{1/8%tsp}, @pepper{1/8%tsp}, and @olive oil{3%tbsp} in a #food processor{} until combined.

Add the @cherry tomatoes{1%cup}(halved) and crispy bacon to the massaged kale, drizzle with the dressing, and toss to combine. Top with optional sliced avocado, crumbled feta or blue cheese, and sweet corn if desired.
